@tradition running
// Gym club (renamed from Running club; id unchanged). Every kind of machine; you count as a member, so any machine you
// tap is yours. Replace the old words with these.
== mail
- Gym club at {time} in the gym. Every machine's in use, and there's always one for you. Soup after. That's the rule.
== ask
- Gym club tonight. There's a machine with your name on it.
- Coming to Gym club? Bikes, rowers, treadmills. Pick one.
== here
- Pace yourself. No, slower. No, that's stopped.   #funny
- Swap with me after this one? I want the rower.
- Nearly done. Soup's waiting.
== thanks
- You join Gym club. Every machine is whirring, someone counts down the last minute, and there's soup after.
== chatter
- Gym club tonight. Then soup. In that order.   #funny
- I went to Gym club for the soup. Stayed for the soup.   #funny
- Gym club's busier than ever. Good.
